abstract: >-
  The Steiner diversities of planar graphs cannot be embedded in L1 with
  bounded distortion. The unit diamond graph D_d is planar, has treewidth two
  and has (2*4^d+4)/3 vertices, and its Steiner diversity needs L1 distortion
  at least (6d+7+2/4^d)/9. With an upper bound of Bryant and Tupper the order
  log n is correct. In flow-cut terms, D_d carries set demands that pass every
  cut test but need at least that congestion when routed by Steiner trees.
  The exact distortion is not determined for d >= 3, and novelty is not
  established.
